A||||5||BlackGT||Replacing my Engine!
Z||000000||BlackGT||08-10-99||07:08 AM||||Ok Folks!<br>After buying my car about 2 weeks ago the engine let go! The sounds I was listening<br>to were that of an engine on it`s last legs<br>after I drove it 500 miles home. My question<br>is as follows...I could get a brand new rebuilt engine (2.8l) or substitute for a<br>few dollars more a new rebuilt 3.1L. I would<br>like to have more power/torque than the origional engine has so I`m leaning towards<br>the 3.1 liter engine, it`s just that I want<br>to make sure there are no surprises when my<br>mechanic does the swap. Me not having access<br>to the tools I would need to do it my self<br>I`m having a mechanic I trust do the swap for<br>me. The engine will cost me about a thousand<br>my mechanic suggests putting in a new clutch<br>and waterpump while he`s in there and he will<br>charge me $800 for his labor. All together I`m looking at $2000 before I can drive it again. What do you guys think? I specified<br>that the engine had to be the 3.1 with the<br>cast heads since I`ve read elsewhere in the<br>forum that this was the correct engine to bolt up to the 4speed tranny and all the other accessories. Is there anything I`m not<br>factoring in on this adventure? Thanks guys!<br> 
Z||000001||BlackGT||08-10-99||07:53 AM||||One more thing guys,<br>This engine is an 89 - 94 3.1liter/189 ci<br>engine with cast heads...this is the right<br>engine..correct?
Z||000002||Cooter||08-10-99||09:52 AM||||I thought that you had to use the fiero heads on the 3.1 to make the intake fit. THe aluminum head motors used a different piston and the port location is not the same as the fiero's is. I have not heard (or read) if the iron head 3.1 uses the same port locations as the 2.8. Hopefully someone will come to your rescue. I would hate to think that you bought a whole 3.1 motor and now might have to pull the heads and use your old ones.
Z||000003||PaUL||08-10-99||03:05 PM||||Hey Cooter, he said "cast heads". The 3.1 came with both cast and al.
Z||000004||Cooter||08-10-99||07:39 PM||||Thank you paul, but that did not answer the question. I figured out that the 3.1 came with both al and cast, but will he need to use the fiero heads to match the factory intake?
Z||000005||PaUL||08-10-99||07:58 PM||||No he wont need it. All cast iron heads have the same port spacing.
